{"name":"Surf’s Surprise","hex":"#c4d3e5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"surf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Waves that break on an ocean shoreline.","An instance or session of riding a surfboard in the surf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ride a wave on a surfboard; to pursue or take part in the sport of surfing.","To surf at a specified place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surf"},{"term":"surprise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something unexpected.","A mess of feces, left by a pet or small child in an unexpected place or at an unexpected time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (someone) to feel unusually alarmed or delighted by something unexpected.","To do something to (a person) that they are not expecting, as a surprise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surprise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Surprise","blocks":[{"text":"Surprise is a rapid, fleeting mental and physiological state. It is related to the startle response experienced by animals and humans as the result of an unexpected event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Charles_Bell%2C_Essays_on_the_anatomy_of_Wellcome_L0031951.jpg/330px-Charles_Bell%2C_Essays_on_the_anatomy_of_Wellcome_L0031951.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surprise","wikidata":"Q333173"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/500px-STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/1280px-STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/STS-51L_riadiace_stredisko.jpg/500px-STS-51L_riadiace_stredi